+# Context teardown
+
+## Requirements
+
+### Complete teardown despite failures
+
+When a request or application context is popped, Flask attempts every
+registered teardown callback and the corresponding teardown signal even if an
+earlier teardown action raises. After cleanup, Flask raises all collected
+teardown errors as an exception group when the runtime supports exception
+groups; otherwise it may raise the first collected error. Context-local state
+is restored before the error escapes.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- D-17: teardown errors are collected across callbacks and teardown signals;
+  cleanup and context restoration take precedence over immediate propagation.
